# Minecraft Version(s): 26.3
## Market prices
- *"How much should I sell diamonds for?"*, *"what's a good price for oak logs?"*, *"what's this worth?"* (the item in your hand): with the Nice Control Center's market, Merl tells you what it sold for lately and what it's listed for now, and suggests a price per item and per lot ("For how many" in /market). Switch it off with **priceAdvice**

## Land claims
- *"Where's my claim?"* now knows the Nice Control Center's land claims (when they're switched on there): your nearest claim, one you're a member of, or one by its name or owner ("my farm claim", "Steve's claim"), with **[Guide me]**. Get Off My Lawn still works when it's the one installed
- When you have no claim yet, Merl tells you to use `/claim mode` instead of placing a claim anchor

## Server rules
- With the Nice Control Center, Merl also knows the server's own rules: the switched-on performance tweaks (*"why did my items disappear so fast?"*, *"is there a mob limit per chunk?"*, *"do far away mobs move slower?"*), the world borders (*"how big is the permanent area?"*) and how land claims work (*"how many claim blocks do I get?"*). Switch it off with **settingsServerRules**

## Discord
- The Discord: JustSync fix is gone: the server now uses the Nice Control Center's Discord bridge, which never shows /merl questions on Discord
